<GuidePageShell
  slug="kitten-feeding-schedule"
  title="Kitten Feeding Schedule by Age"
  description="Kitten feeding schedule by age: meals per day, weaning notes, calorie multipliers, and when orphan or underweight kittens need a vet."
  answer="A kitten feeding schedule matches meal frequency and calories to age: nursing on demand early, then about three to four meals daily after weaning, often two meals by adulthood. Use a growth diet and a kitten energy factor (commonly ~2.5 × RER) as a starting estimate. Weigh often and call your veterinarian for poor weight gain, diarrhea, or orphan feeding plans."
  takeaways={[
    'Weaned kittens commonly need 3–4 meals/day; many taper toward 2 meals near adulthood.',
    'Feed complete growth diets until about 12 months (ask your vet about large breeds).',
    'Starting calories: RER ≈ 70 × kg^0.75, then × ~2.5 for many kittens.',
    'Example: 1.5 kg kitten ≈ 95 kcal RER → ~237 kcal/day before treat adjustments.',
    'Do not give cow’s milk; orphan feeding plans belong with a veterinarian.',
    'Neutering lowers needs—recalculate portions instead of free-feeding forever.',
    'Use the cat food calculator (kitten stage) and cat age calculator alongside this schedule.',
  ]}
  faq={faq}
